ient evidence to support the allegation of Physical Abuse, which resulted in a child being injured while in care.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026604600","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1479251-i20260715-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-701-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1479251-i20260715","date":"2026-07-15","original_code":"746.701(5)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-09-04","finding":"Licensing Incident/Illness Report Form - Situations Placing Children at Risk: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, there is sufficient evidence to support the operation did not have an incident report available for review regarding an incident that involved staff using inappropriate physical discipline that resulted in a child being injured.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026604598","violation_type_title":"Licensing Incident/Illness Report Form - Situations Placing Children at Risk (26 TAC §746.701(5))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1479251-i20260715-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1305-a-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1479251-i20260715","date":"2026-07-15","original_code":"746.1305(a)(3)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-09-04","finding":"Pre-service Training- Discipline and Guidance: Based on the DFPS investigation, it was found that the permit holder, acting in the role of a caregiver, did not receive discipline and guidance training prior to providing care for children.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026604596","violation_type_title":"Pre-service Training- Discipline and Guidance (26 TAC §746.1305(a)(3))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":